Z||000000||Richard Parnell||04-20-2000||09:35 PM||||Last weekend a buddy and I were scrambling around junkyards looking for parts and came across a strange looking vehicle.  It was about the size of an old VW bug, it was a convertible (no top left), front engined (no engine).  It had no name on it but did have some kind of coat of arms on the steering wheel center(English looking) and most amazing of all it was completely sanded and didn't have a bit of rust on the body which was stainless steel.  I could only come up with the name Wauxall (spelling?) from somewhere in the recesses of my mind.  Any ideas what it is?  If I have to I'll go back and take a pic of it.  It had the frame still together also.||||reg||5
Z||000001||daved||04-20-2000||10:31 PM||||The English GM car make is a Vauxall.  But as far as I know, only the Delorean had a SS body.  You sure it was SS...maybe Aluminum?<BR>Never heard of that either...but you never know. D.||||reg||1
